.SH NAME
kitrepo \- a table in the xCAT database.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBkitrepo Attributes:\fR  \fIkitreponame\fR, \fIkitname\fR, \fIosbasename\fR, \fIosmajorversion\fR, \fIosminorversion\fR, \fIosarch\fR, \fIcompat_osbasenames\fR, \fIkitrepodir\fR, \fIcomments\fR, \fIdisable\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This table stores all kits added to the xCAT cluster.
.SH "kitrepo Attributes:"
.IX Header "kitrepo Attributes:"
.IP \fBkitreponame\fR 10
.IX Item "kitreponame"
The unique generated kit repo package name, when kit is added to the cluster.
.IP \fBkitname\fR 10
.IX Item "kitname"
The Kit name which this Kit Package Repository belongs to.
.IP \fBosbasename\fR 10
.IX Item "osbasename"
The OS distro name which this repository is based on.
.IP \fBosmajorversion\fR 10
.IX Item "osmajorversion"
The OS distro major version which this repository is based on.
.IP \fBosminorversion\fR 10
.IX Item "osminorversion"
The OS distro minor version which this repository is based on. If this attribute is not set, it means that this repo applies to all minor versions.
.IP \fBosarch\fR 10
.IX Item "osarch"
The OS distro arch which this repository is based on.
.IP \fBcompat_osbasenames\fR 10
.IX Item "compat_osbasenames"
List of compatible OS base names.
.IP \fBkitrepodir\fR 10
.IX Item "kitrepodir"
The path to Kit Repository directory on the Mgt Node.
.IP \fBcomments\fR 10
.IX Item "comments"
Any user-written notes.
.IP \fBdisable\fR 10
.IX Item "disable"
Set to 'yes' or '1' to comment out this row.
